  "body": "Nowadays, all browsers allow users to copy the address of a link. However, the address in `href` may not be the best one to copy. Authors may sometimes want user to get a different link, e.g. the short url, or the real url behind a track and/or short url.\n\nI suggest adding an attribute to link elements which presents a canonical address of the target that the browser can use when user wants to copy the link.\n\nOne concern is that, it could be confusing sometims that the address you copy is not the same address in the location bar after you click the link. Websites may also abuse this feature. Not sure whether it would have any security concerns.\n\nThoughts?\n",
